#, fuzzy
msgid "Dynamic class loading"
msgstr "Carga dinámica de clases"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`Class.forName()`, `ClassLoader.loadClass()`, and `MethodHandles.Lookup."
"findClass()` calls where the class name is a string constant in the bytecode."
" For cases where class names are constructed at runtime (e.g., via "
"`StringBuilder` or `invokedynamic` string concatenation), the tree-shaker "
"traces the call chain up to the class whose constructor or static "
"initializer triggers the loading, then executes it in a forked JVM with an "
"isolated class loader to dynamically capture which classes are loaded. This "
"handles libraries like BouncyCastle that build class names from package "
"prefixes and algorithm name arrays."
msgstr ""
"`Class.forName()` , `ClassLoader.loadClass()` , y `MethodHandles.Lookup."
"findClass()` llamadas en las que el nombre de la clase es una constante de "
"cadena en el código de bytes. Para los casos en los que los nombres de clase "
"se construyen en tiempo de ejecución (por ejemplo, mediante la concatenación "
"de cadenas `StringBuilder` o `invokedynamic` ), el árbol rastrea la cadena "
"de llamadas hasta la clase cuyo constructor o inicializador estático "
"desencadena la carga y, a continuación, la ejecuta en una JVM bifurcada con "
"un cargador de clases aislado para capturar dinámicamente qué clases se "
"cargan. Esto maneja bibliotecas como BouncyCastle que construyen nombres de "
"clases a partir de prefijos de paquetes y matrices de nombres de algoritmos."

#, fuzzy
msgid "Reflection, JNI, and service provider registrations"
msgstr "Registros de Reflection, JNI y proveedores de servicios"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Classes registered by extensions for reflection (`ReflectiveClassBuildItem`, "
"`ReflectiveFieldBuildItem`, `ReflectiveMethodBuildItem`), JNI runtime access "
"(`JniRuntimeAccessBuildItem`, `JniRuntimeAccessFieldBuildItem`, "
"`JniRuntimeAccessMethodBuildItem`), and service providers "
"(`ServiceProviderBuildItem`) are treated as root classes, see <<root-"
"collection>>. Weak reflective registrations are excluded — they are only "
"preserved if bytecode analysis independently reaches them. Conditional "
"registrations (`ReflectiveClassConditionBuildItem`) are evaluated to a fixed "
"point: a conditionally registered class becomes a root only when its "
"condition type is reachable."
msgstr ""
"Las clases registradas por extensiones para la reflexión ( "
"`ReflectiveClassBuildItem` , `ReflectiveFieldBuildItem` , "
"`ReflectiveMethodBuildItem` ), el acceso en tiempo de ejecución a JNI ( "
"`JniRuntimeAccessBuildItem` , `JniRuntimeAccessFieldBuildItem` , "
"`JniRuntimeAccessMethodBuildItem` ) y los proveedores de servicios ( "
"`ServiceProviderBuildItem` ) se tratan como clases raíz; véase <<root-"
"collection>> . Se excluyen los registros reflexivos débiles: solo se "
"conservan si el análisis del código byte llega a ellos de forma "
"independiente. Los registros condicionales ( "
"`ReflectiveClassConditionBuildItem` ) se evalúan hasta un punto fijo: una "
"clase registrada de forma condicional solo se convierte en raíz cuando se "
"puede acceder a su tipo de condición."

#, fuzzy
msgid "String constants"
msgstr "Constantes de cadena"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When a method contains a string constant that exactly matches a fully-"
"qualified dependency class name, that class is marked reachable. Comma- or "
"colon-delimited lists of class names (as used by some frameworks) are also "
"handled by splitting and matching each part."
msgstr ""
"Cuando un método contiene una constante de cadena que coincide exactamente "
"con un nombre de clase de dependencia totalmente cualificado, esa clase se "
"marca como alcanzable. Las listas de nombres de clases delimitadas por comas "
"o dos puntos (como las que utilizan algunos frameworks) también se manejan "
"dividiendo y haciendo coincidir cada parte."

msgid "Enclosing classes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a nested class is reachable, its enclosing class is preserved, because "
"`Class.getSimpleName()`, `Class.getEnclosingClass()` and `Class."
"getDeclaringClass()` load it. The enclosing class is only made loadable — "
"its own code is not traced, so the classes it references are not preserved "
"by this rule alone. The relationship is read from the `InnerClasses` and "
"`EnclosingMethod` attributes rather than guessed from the `$` in the class "
"name, so a top-level class that merely has a `$` in its name preserves "
"nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Member classes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A reachable class keeps the member classes it declares. They are made "
"loadable without tracing their code, so the classes *they* reference are not "
"preserved by this rule alone. The relationship is read from the "
"`InnerClasses` attribute, so a top-level class that merely has a `$` in its "
"name keeps nothing. This rule exists because member classes are routinely "
"enumerated reflectively — `Class.getDeclaredClasses()`, `Class."
"getClasses()`, and the class queries `native-image` performs for every type "
"registered for reflection — and such an enumeration cannot be traced back to "
"a particular receiver class. An extension can additionally require the "
"member classes of a class that is *not* otherwise reachable with "
"`JarTreeShakeDeclaredClassesBuildItem`; `native-image` needs this to resolve "
"a `@TargetClass(innerClass = ...)` substitution target."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "Multi-release JAR entries"
msgstr "Entradas JAR multilanzamiento"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`META-INF/versions/N/` entries are analyzed, picking the highest version "
"compatible with the application's target Java version. Entries targeting "
"newer Java versions are also preserved when they are referenced by reachable "
"higher-version code, ensuring the JAR works correctly when run on a newer "
"JVM (e.g., native image built with Mandrel 25 while the app was compiled "
"with JDK 21)."
msgstr ""
"`META-INF/versions/N/` se analizan las entradas, eligiendo la versión más "
"alta compatible con la versión Java objetivo de la aplicación. Las entradas "
"que apuntan a versiones más recientes de Java también se conservan cuando "
"son referenciadas por código alcanzable de versión superior, lo que "
"garantiza que el JAR funciona correctamente cuando se ejecuta en una JVM más "
"reciente (por ejemplo, una imagen nativa construida con Mandrel 25 mientras "
"que la aplicación se compiló con JDK 21)."

#, fuzzy
msgid "JBoss Logging companions"
msgstr "Compañeros de registro de JBoss"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`_$logger` and `_$bundle` companion classes are automatically included when "
"their owning class is reachable."
msgstr ""
"`_$logger_` _y <code></code>_ `$bundle` clases acompañantes se incluyen "
"automáticamente cuando su clase propietaria es alcanzable."

#, fuzzy
msgid "Sisu named components"
msgstr "Componentes con nombre Sisu"

#, fuzzy
